Just had one of the best confrontations I've had in a long while...

possible spoilers

Wyvin the Chaotic Elf has got Stormbringer and being true to
nature doesn't care who she kills. Sacrificed an elf at my
altar and peaceful Yeenoghu was summoned. I tried to avoid it,
but inevitably I hit it. I had AC -9, the sword was +1 and
I had gauntlets of power. I was fast, but no speed boots for
extra speed. I had reflection and magic resistance.

Yeenoghu's method of attack is to hit once with a barrage of
stuff until you hit it. Then it teleports away and comes back
fully healed. Did between 10-20 HP damage per attack (I had 98
HP max). I eventually discovered that the demon retreats to the
up staircase to heal, so here's what I did:

Engrave Elbereth with wand of digging and fend off Y until
fully healed. Make a break for the stairs until HP are getting
dangerously low then engrave again and heal. Keep doing this
until the stairs. Once next to the stairs, you can repeatedly
hit the demon. Unfortunately I wasn't _on_ the stairs so the
demon escaped upstairs and I had to repeat the procedure on
the next level up. This time I sat on the stairs, with Elbereth,
and nailed Yeenoghu (having previously used up my magic marker and
all my blessed blank scrolls to make +7 Stormy and AC -11).

I was still a low level character, so I couldn't do things like
teleport with control, cast spells reliably, or even levitate to
prevent scuffing my engraving. Used a lot of digging charges!
A very satisfying battle.

Derek

